      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'd like to be able to save multiple recolorings of the same avatar as if they're different avatars in my favorites, so I can swap between them easily (and of course, not lose the colorings when changing worlds).  I'd prefer to see this separated from \"Expressions\" into a dedicated \"Customizations\" area, so that expression animations remain quick-access, and customizations are all grouped together.  It would also make more sense to display certain customizations as a toggle rather than the icon making them seem like a playing animation (even if they are) for less user confusion.  \"Save how I look now and keep it permanently\" seems like an important aspect of how players experience avatar customizations.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
